Administrator "1" -- "0..*" TrainingMaterial : manages
Administrator "1" -- "0..*" Quiz : manages
Quiz "1" *-- "1..*" Question : contains

## 7. Relationships Between Classes

- **User – QuizAttempt:** One user can make multiple quiz attempts.
- **QuizAttempt – Quiz:** Each quiz attempt is associated with a quiz.
- **Quiz – Question:** A quiz contains one or more questions.
- **User – Progress:** A user can have multiple progress records or updates.
- **User – Feedback:** A user may receive multiple feedback records.
- **User – TrainingMaterial:** Users can access multiple training materials.
- **User – PhishingSimulation:** Users can participate in multiple simulations.
- **Administrator – TrainingMaterial:** An administrator manages training materials.
- **Administrator – Quiz:** An administrator manages quizzes.
- **Quiz – Question:** Composition represents questions as parts of a quiz in this proposed model.

## 8. Industry Mapping: Object-Oriented System Design

Class Diagram modeling supports Object-Oriented System Design by defining the system's classes, responsibilities, and relationships before implementation.

For the proposed platform, the model separates user management, learning content, phishing simulations, assessments, progress tracking, and feedback into distinct classes. This separation can improve modularity, maintainability, and future extensibility.

## 9. Observation

Object-Oriented Analysis helps convert functional requirements into classes and relationships. UML Class Diagram modeling provides a structured view of the proposed system's static architecture.

## 10. Result

The major classes, attributes, methods, and relationships of the proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform were identified, and a text-based UML Class Diagram was prepared as part of Object-Oriented System Design.

**Note:** This is a proposed design model. The classes and methods should be validated against the actual implementation before being described as implemented features.